name:"San Fernando Valley, Santa Clarita<br /> & Beyond",id:"sfv-more",zoom:"300%,32%,0%",content:'\n        <div class="main-page">\n          <figure class="page-img" style="max-width: 450px; float: left; margin: 0 30px 10px 0">\n            <img class="photo" src="images/la/sfv-more/soraya.jpg" alt="Large concert hall viewed from upper deck" />\n            <figcaption>\n              <span>The Soraya at Cal State Northridge (CSUN)</span> <span><i class="fa-solid fa-camera" title=", Photo by:"></i> Tim Paik</span>\n            </figcaption>\n          </figure>\n\n          <p>Called exclusively "<strong>the Valley</strong>" over LA\'s many other valleys, the <strong>San Fernando Valley</strong> is perhaps the most iconic LA suburbia. Its image as LA\'s quintessential suburbs has been shaped by decades of TV and film, often focusing on its mall culture, car-centric life, and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_girl" target="_blank">Valley Girl <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" title="Opens in a new tab"></i></a> persona. While other LA suburban areas consist of independent cities or unincorporated areas, most of the Valley is officially <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Fernando_Valley#City_of_Los_Angeles_neighborhoods_of_the_San_Fernando_Valley" target="_blank">part of the city of LA <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" title="Opens in a new tab"></i></a>, creating a closer connection with the city\'s culture and identity. Also unlike many LA suburbs, the Valley sits closer to <a href="#la/central-la/hollywood">Hollywood</a> rather than <a href="#la/central-la/dtla">Downtown LA</a>, making it a natural home base for studios and those in Hollywood\'s entertainment industries. Even local performing arts venues here, like <a href="https://thesoraya.org/en/" target="_blank">CSUN\'s Soraya <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" title="Opens in a new tab"></i></a></a>, are often a popular stop for world-famous artists touring in LA.</p>\n\n          <hr />\n\n          <figure class="page-img" style="max-width: 450px; float: right; margin: 0 0 20px 30px">\n            <img class="photo" src="images/la/sfv-more/wat-thai.jpg" alt="Colorful street food vendors selling Thai food" />\n            <figcaption>\n              <span class="standard">Thai food stalls at North Hollywood\'s Wat Thai Temple</span>\n              <span class="mobile">Food stalls at Wat Thai Temple</span>\n              <span><i class="fa-solid fa-camera" title=", Photo by:"></i> Tim Paik</span>\n            </figcaption>\n          </figure>\n\n          <p>The region, however, has much more to offer beyond its suburban connection to the film and entertainment industries of Hollywood. Reflecting LA and its cosmopolitan culture, the Valley is also home to a multicultural and open-minded population, most notably with a thriving food scene that celebrates diversity.</p>\n          <p>Offering one of the few permanent open-air food markets in LA besides <a href="#la/central-la/fairfax-beverly-grove">Farmers Market on 3rd</a> and <a href="#la/central-la/dtla">Smorgasburg</a>, the <a href="#la/sfv-more/noho">Wat Thai Temple located in North Hollywood</a> is a prime example. As LA\'s largest Thai Buddhist temple, Wat Thai serves as a gathering place every weekend for LA\'s Thai community, with food vendors that also welcome Angelenos of all backgrounds from across the city with some of the most authentic and affordable Thai food that rivals <a href="#la/central-la/east-hollywood">East Hollywood\'s Thai Town in Central LA</a>.</p>\n\n          <hr style="margin-bottom: 20px;"/>\n\n          <p>Around its western edges, the Valley also boasts direct access to some of LA\'s most untouched and unique nature, like the rolling hills of the <a href="#la/sfv-more/woodland-hills-west-hills">Upper Las Virgenes Canyon in Woodland Hills</a> and <a href="#la/sfv-more/chatsworth">Cretaceous Period sandstone formations in Chatsworth</a>. Bordering the Valley to the north is yet another pair of valley communities of LA County: <strong href="#la/sfv-more/scv-castaic-av">Santa Clarita Valley</strong> \u2013 home to one of LA\'s newer suburban developments and Castaic Lake \u2013 and the <strong href="#la/sfv-more/scv-castaic-av">Antelope Valley</strong>, known for its Mojave desert landscapes and California Poppy Reserve.</p>\n\n          <hr />\n\n          <figure class="page-img" style="max-width: 1000px; margin-top: 5px;">\n            <img class="photo standard" src="images/la/sfv-more/woodland-hills.jpg" alt="Rolling hills with grassy fields" />\n            <img class="photo mobile" src="images/la/sfv-more/woodland-hills-mobile.jpg" alt="Rolling hills with grassy fields" />\n            <figcaption>\n              <span class="standard">Upper Las Virgenes Canyon in Woodland Hills, one of LA\'s most pristine open space nature preserves with expansive trails</span>\n              <span class="mobile">Upper Las Virgenes Canyon, Woodland Hills</span>\n              <span><i class="fa-solid fa-camera" title=", Photo by:"></i> Tim Paik</span>\n            </figcaption>\n          </figure>\n\n          <div class="construction" style="margin-top: 30px;">\n            <hr style="margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px;" />\n            <h3 class="item-links-title" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><i class="fa-solid fa-map-location-dot"></i> Keep Exploring</h3>\n            <hr style="margin-bottom: 20px;" />\n            <ul>\n              <li><a href="#la/central-la">Central LA</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/westside-more">Westside & Beyond</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/south-bay-harbor">South Bay & Harbor</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/catalina">Catalina</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/south-la-gateway-cities">South LA & More</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/eastside-nela">Eastside & NELA</a></li>\n              <li><a href="#la/sgv-more">SGV & Beyond</a></li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      ',
